## Method

### Task 1: Data cleaning and chart preparation

The file had no blank cells, because missing values had already been replaced with the text "Not Given". Cleaning therefore focused on hidden problems:

| Check | Finding | Action |
|---|---|---|
| Duplicate records | 4 records repeated under a different `show_id` (s5965, s5966, s5967, s6530) | Removed the later copy of each |
| Non-breaking space | "Consequences" ended with character 160, which Excel `TRIM` does not remove | Cleaned with `SUBSTITUTE(...,CHAR(160)," ")` |
| Line break in a title | s8420 splits into two rows in some imports, creating a false third type "William Wyler" and a total of 8,791 | Replaced with a space |
| Titles turned into dates | "22-Jul", "15-Aug", "1-Oct" | Restored to "22 July", "15 August", "October 1" ("9-Feb" could not be verified and was left unchanged) |
| Country placeholder | 421 titles say "Pakistan"; 402 of them have an unknown director (95.5%, against 26% for the US), and include Squid Game and Chicago Party Aunt | 401 records (after de-duplication) reclassified to "Not Given"; original kept in `Country_Original` |
| Dates and types | `date_added` converted to real dates; type vs duration and rating codes checked | No errors found |

Result: **8,790 raw records became 8,786 clean records.** Four pivot-style tables and four basic charts are on `T1_Pivots`.

> **Why the duplicates are easy to miss:** Excel's default Remove Duplicates compares every column, including `show_id`, which always differs. Untick `show_id` when running it.

### Task 2: Content distribution dashboard
Pie, column and clustered-column charts with six KPI tiles. Movie length uses `AVERAGEIFS`, `MINIFS` and `MAXIFS` on a numeric duration helper column.

### Task 3: Country-wise dashboard
Top 20 countries ranked with `COUNTIFS`, a dropdown Type filter, conditional formatting for the top three, and a region roll-up (the region mapping is an editable analyst assumption). "Not Given" is excluded from ranking.

### Task 4: Release trend visualization
Titles by release year and by year added, with year-over-year growth, cumulative growth, 2016 to 2019 CAGR and decade tables.

### Task 5: Audience rating insights
The 14 rating codes are grouped into five audience groups (Kids, Older Kids/Family, Teens, Adults, Unrated) through the `Lookups` sheet. Five KPI tiles and filtered charts.

### Task 6: Executive dashboard
Consolidates Tasks 1 to 5 on one screen with six KPIs, four charts, one filter and the recommendations.

